From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:47:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/38] Make buttons with button styles on Linux

Button draws through the nearest buttonStyle, PrimitiveButtonStyle or
ButtonStyle, with the label as the style's configuration.label, its role
and the pressed state while a finger is down. The system styles look as
on iOS: automatic and borderless in the tint (red when destructive),
plain, bordered and borderedProminent with the control size and the
border shape. A disabled button is gray and does nothing. Buttons get the
role and system image initializers and Button(configuration).

A view alias counts as unknown when its source is not in the count
inputs, which a graph inputs modifier does not write to: counting it as
nothing dropped buttons from lists.
